Upstream-Status: Backport [sched_attr.h: use compat struct when kernel headers lack SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1]

On Linux 4.19, linux/sched/types.h defines only SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER0 (48 bytes)
and the struct sched_attr lacks sched_util_min/sched_util_max.  glibc's own
compat struct (in bits/sched.h) includes those fields but is guarded by
"#ifndef SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER0" -- which is already set by the kernel header,
so it is skipped.

util-linux's sched_attr.h also has a compat struct but only activates when
HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR is unset (i.e. glibc doesn't provide the syscall wrapper).
On modern glibc HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR IS set, so that path is also skipped, and
uclampset.c ends up with a struct sched_attr that has no sched_util_min/max.

Fix: also activate the compat struct when SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1 is absent.
SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1 (= 56) was added to linux/sched/types.h in Linux 5.0
together with the uclamp fields, so its absence reliably indicates an old
kernel header that lacks the uclamp struct members.

Signed-off-by: Yocto wrynose migration

diff --git a/schedutils/sched_attr.h b/schedutils/sched_attr.h
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/schedutils/sched_attr.h
+++ b/schedutils/sched_attr.h
@@ -81,7 +81,13 @@ static int sched_getattr(pid_t pid, struct sched_attr *attr, unsigned int size,
 #endif
 
-#if defined (__linux__) && !defined(HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR) && defined(SYS_sched_setattr)
-# define HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR
+/* Also use the compat struct when HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR is set but the kernel
+ * headers lack SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1 (added in Linux 5.0 alongside
+ * sched_util_min/sched_util_max).  This happens on kernel 4.19 where
+ * linux/sched/types.h only defines SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER0.
+ */
+#if defined (__linux__) && (!defined(HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR) || !defined(SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER1)) && defined(SYS_sched_setattr)
+# ifdef HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR
+#  undef HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR
+# endif
+# define HAVE_SCHED_SETATTR
